## Core architecture — three separate layers, deliberately decoupled
1. **Schema** (ACF fields + CPT UI taxonomies) — lives in local
   MySQL only, NOT in git at all.
2. **Public-facing website** (`main_display.php`, `page-*.php`
   templates) — reads schema via `get_field()`, purely reductive:
   only renders fields that have values. Never dictates what the
   schema contains.
3. **Office UI** (ACF Location Rules / Conditional Logic) — controls
   what Authors see while editing, independent of what's shown
   publicly. A field can be hidden in the editor but still render
   publicly if it has a saved value (and vice versa).

These three are intentionally decoupled — changes to one shouldn't
force changes to the others. Keep it that way.

## Key files
- `functions.php` — theme setup, all custom functions. Contains:
  - `oswp_forty_start()` / `oswp_forty_end()` — the Forty shell
    wrapper (header/nav/footer). Every Forty-based page/template
    calls these at top/bottom.
  - `oswp_page_start()` / `oswp_page_end()` — OLD Twenty Twenty-Five
    shell wrapper, only for un-migrated pages.
  - `oswp_get_event_record($post_id)` — single source of truth for
    an event's full data: all ACF fields + staff/venue/event_category
    taxonomy terms, merged into one flat array.
  - `oswp_render_tile_row()` — reusable helper, renders a row of N
    tiles at a given Forty width class, but ONLY if count matches
    exactly (silent skip otherwise).
  - `single_template` filter — routes the `event` post type to
    `main_display.php` regardless of filename (doesn't rely on
    WordPress's `single-event.php` naming convention).
  - Image sizes registered: `event-featured` (800x450, 16:9),
    `oswp-square` (800x800, 1:1), `oswp-landscape` (1067x800, 4:3).
  - `remove_post_type_support('event', 'editor')` — WYSIWYG fully
    disabled for events, confirmed team decision. Content is 100%
    ACF-driven for events.
- `main_display.php` — the main event template (renamed from
  `page-duplex.php` mid-project; "Duplex"/"four square" were dev
  codenames, no longer used). Vertical order: h1 → tagline →
  featured_image (optional) → main_tile_image (optional, exactly 2)
  → small_tile_image (optional, exactly 3) → two-column (LH
  event_summary / RH event_details) → action buttons (ticket/RSVP/
  enquiry links).
- `page-billboard.php` — homepage tile/billboard template. Tile
  content currently placeholder (6 Karamu-style tiles, all linking
  to `/ipsum/`) — real tile targets not yet decided. NOT yet
  promoted to actual homepage (`front-page.php` / `show_on_front`
  still points at old page ID 55).
- `page-recurring.php` — "Regular Events" listing page. Migrated
  tonight from broken `get_header()/get_footer()` (was silently
  using WP's ugly compat template) to proper Forty shell. Loops all
  recurring events, shows title/tagline/schedule sentence, optional
  `avatar` field (new, fixed-size square image on RH side, kept
  deliberately separate from main_display.php's tile logic).
- `custom.css` — user's own file, being actively reorganised by user
  (not Claude) going forward. Loads at priority 22 (after Forty's
  main.css at 21) — this load-order fix was a real bug hunt tonight,
  don't reintroduce.
- `style.css` — minimal required child-theme header (Theme Name/
  Template/Description) — WordPress won't recognise the theme
